.TH SHEDMAN-CONFIG 1 "2026-04-25" "ShedOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shedman-config \- sync packaged dotfile defaults and review merge conflicts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shedman config
.RB { -s | --sync }
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B shedman config
.RB { -r | --review }
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shedman config
is an umbrella for the two dotfile-related operations on ShedOS:
.B --sync
seeds packaged defaults into
.B $HOME
and runs a per-file 3-way merge after every upgrade;
.B --review
opens the IntelliJ-style merge TUI for unresolved
.I .shedosnew
conflicts.
.SH SUBMODES
.TP
.BR -s , " --sync"
Run the 3-way merge between pristine defaults
(under
.IR /usr/share/shedos/<pkg>/defaults/ ),
your live
.B $HOME
files, and the manifest at
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/shedos/last-seen/ .
Files you've edited are never overwritten — when both you and
upstream changed a file, the upstream version lands as
.IR <file>.shedosnew .
.IP
Common flags (forwarded to the underlying tool):
.B --dry-run
print plan, change nothing;
.B --yes
skip prompts;
.B --rebuild-manifest
re-hash current $HOME against current defaults (used after
manually-resolving a conflict).
.TP
.BR -r , " --review"
Open the merge TUI for every
.I .shedosnew
sidecar in
.B $HOME .
Per-hunk decisions: y (yours), t (theirs), b (both YT), B (both
TY), x (skip), u (undo). Whole-file shortcuts: A (all yours), T
(all theirs). Save with
.B s
\(em atomic; the previous live file is backed up to
.IR <file>.shedosbak .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/shedos/<pkg>/defaults/
Pristine defaults shipped by each package.
.TP
.I $HOME/<file>.shedosnew
Upstream version of a file you've also edited locally.
.TP
.I $HOME/<file>.shedosbak
Backup of the pre-merge YOURS file (lossless).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/shedos/last-seen/
Manifest tracking the per-file hash of the last default version
seen.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/shedos/sync-exclude
Optional glob list of files to opt out of declarative management.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shedman (1),
.BR shedman-update (1).
